abstract: >-
  Prophages are viruses that are integrated into bacterial genomes. A few computational biologists
  are keen to identify those specific regions, because they are more interesting than the rest of the
  genome. For more about prophages, take a look at the home pages for some of the tools listed here.

  This site is not intended to be a gentle introduction to prophages, but a FAIR (findable,
  accessible, interoperable, and reusable) data resource for comparing prophage prediction software.
